<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Desktop pick-and-place arm on Trayson Rubio</title><link>https://traysonr.github.io/x/projects/robot-arm/</link><description>Recent content in Desktop pick-and-place arm on Trayson Rubio</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 11:20:00 -0700</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://traysonr.github.io/x/projects/robot-arm/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Repeatability test with a printed target grid</title><link>https://traysonr.github.io/x/projects/robot-arm/updates/2026-04-02-repeatability-test/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 11:20:00 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://traysonr.github.io/x/projects/robot-arm/updates/2026-04-02-repeatability-test/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I ran ten approach cycles at five points on a paper target grid. The arm returns within roughly 4 mm near the center of the workspace; error grows near full extension as joint flex and servo backlash accumulate.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="../repeatability.svg" alt="Target grid plot"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Next: stiffen the shoulder bracket and repeat the same sequence. Embed a YouTube video with the shortcode:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;"&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen" loading="eager" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/aqz-KE-bpKQ?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0" style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;" title="YouTube video"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Linkage layout and workspace</title><link>https://traysonr.github.io/x/projects/robot-arm/updates/2026-03-18-linkage-layout/</link><pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 14:00:00 -0700</pubDate><guid>https://traysonr.github.io/x/projects/robot-arm/updates/2026-03-18-linkage-layout/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I settled on a shoulder, elbow, and wrist arrangement with a fixed base rotation. The first CAD pass prioritizes accessible fasteners and keeping the arm light enough for hobby servos.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="control-sketch"&gt;Control sketch&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The initial controller maps target points in the arm plane to two joint angles. I?m keeping the kinematics in a small module so it can be tested independently from the servo driver.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;solve_planar&lt;/span&gt;(x, y, upper, forearm):&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Return shoulder and elbow angles for a reachable point.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; cos_elbow &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; (x&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;x &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; y&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;y &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; upper&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;upper &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; forearm&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;forearm) &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;upper&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;forearm)&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; elbow &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; math&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;acos(max(&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;, min(&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1.0&lt;/span&gt;, cos_elbow)))&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; shoulder &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; math&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;atan2(y, x) &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; math&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;atan2(forearm&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;math&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;sin(elbow), upper &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; forearm&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;math&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;cos(elbow))&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; shoulder, elbow&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>